{"created": "2026-08-19T19:18:33.716855+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-19T19:18:53.090446+00:00", "id": 22017149, "conceptrecid": "22017148", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22017148", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "metadata": {"title": "One Table, Two Regimes: Standard-Model Particles and Condensed-Matter Excitations as Patterns on the Bruhat-Tits Tree", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "publication_date": "2026-08-19", "description": "Physics maintains two particle catalogs that never meet in one framework: the Standard Model's finite table of elementary fermions and bosons, and the open-ended zoo of quasiparticles and anyons discovered in condensed matter. This paper assembles both catalogs into a single pattern table on the Bruhat-Tits tree. The organizing claim is that every entry in both catalogs is a labeled pattern of this one tree, distinguished by a five-field address: place and branch of the tree, node class, Compton count, and statistics phase. Statistics is read as a tree-automorphism phase: bosons carry the trivial phase, fermions the sign phase of an edge half-turn, and abelian anyons the root-of-unity phases that open on ramified branches. The framework's new content is the table, the regime dictionary that says when each reading applies, and falsifiability conditions spanning both catalogs. Its premises end at five named inputs: the Compton count as the only primitive, the tree as the state-space geometry, the exchange-phase invariant for spin-statistics, the rational-function reading of quasiparticle masses, and the p-adic braid phases of abelian anyons. For every known particle the table recapitulates established results; its evidential value lies in the pre-registered address scheme, to be tested against excitations not yet characterized.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Quni-Gudzinas, Rowan Brad", "affiliation": "QNFO", "orcid": "0009-0002-4317-5604"}], "keywords": ["Bruhat-Tits tree", "spin-statistics", "anyons", "quasiparticles", "p-adic physics", "unification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/QNFO/ultrametric-physics/tree/ump/paper/pattern-particle-unification", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v0.1", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22017148"}}]}}, "title": "One Table, Two Regimes: Standard-Model Particles and Condensed-Matter Excitations as Patterns on the Bruhat-Tits Tree", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22017149", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22017149", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22017149?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22017149", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22017149/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22017148", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22017148", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22017148", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22017148", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22017149/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22017149/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149:pattern-particle-unification.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149:pattern-particle-unification.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149:pattern-particle-unification.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22017149:pattern-particle-unific